      "id": "994bf0187afb0197415c9541625419efd64e7dc4",
      "message": "check:standingat \u2014 re-pin the MapScreen exemption after OTA-1816's import\n\nMAINTENANCE OF A STANDING EXCEPTION. One integer, 684 -> 685, plus the\nprovenance beside it. No gate widened, no new exemption, no app source.\n\nOTA-1816 added one import line to MapScreen \u2014 useHumanAction from\nstate/humanActivity, so a TRAVEL TO press accounts the player's activity \u2014\nsix hundred lines above the exempted statement and about nothing but a\ntimestamp. The allowlist is keyed file+line, so the required gate went red on\na statement nobody touched.\n\nBYTE-IDENTICAL, VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSERTED: md5 7614f6948a93f4ea13e5ff102dcf43c4\nat both dec37739:684 and 6c1bda29:685 \u2014 the same hash this file already records\nfor the fourth drift.\n\nThis is the FIFTH drift for the same reason, and the cheapest yet: a single\nimport now costs a red required gate. The text-keyed fix named in this file\nsince the fourth drift is therefore no longer theoretical debt. It is still not\ndone here, for the reason the file itself gives \u2014 widening a gate inside a\nscoped repair is how gates become decoration.\n\n\u26a0 The publication anchor already covers what follows. This is a scripts-only\ncommit behind a bundle change that failed CI, which is exactly the stranded-\nbundle shape OTA-1804 hit on this same gate; the anchor measures from the last\ncommit published to golem, so 6c1bda29's app/ changes stay inside the range.\n\n22/22 gates green, re-run by exit code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
